{{!
    @template tool_vae/import_page

    The page "Importer une fiche", below its heading: the refusal drawn before the form, or the form.

    The template holds no logic: the states exclude one another before, in tool_vae\output\import_page. It has no text of
    its own; it places two keys of HTML made by the core (triple braces): noticehtml, a notification
    ($output->notification()); formhtml, the form of the core (moodleform::render()), drawn once.

    Classes required for JS:
    * none

    Data attributes required for JS:
    * none

    Context variables required for this template:
    * noticehtml - false, or HTML: the refusal drawn instead of the form
    * formhtml - false, or HTML: the form to import a record

    Example context (json):
    {
        "noticehtml": false,
        "formhtml": "<form method=\"post\" action=\"https://example.com/admin/tool/vae/import.php\"></form>"
    }
}}
{{#noticehtml}}
{{{noticehtml}}}
{{/noticehtml}}
{{#formhtml}}
{{{formhtml}}}
{{/formhtml}}
